{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "Thank you, Elena. Here are my coverage findings. My review of the applicable cyber policy, based on the endorsement I received yesterday, confirmed two critical requirements: First, the insurer must receive notice before any court filing is made. Second, the insurer must consent in writing before the company engages an outside forensic expert whose fees will be claimed as covered defense costs. I have not yet circulated my coverage note, but I am disclosing these findings to the group now. This means we cannot proceed with any court filing until the insurer has been put on notice, and if we plan to engage an outside forensic expert and seek reimbursement of those fees as covered defense costs, we must obtain the insurer's written consent first. These notice and consent requirements could directly affect our cost recovery and our timeline."}
```

